 "omitted_tabs": [],
 "gaps": [
  {"concept":"Existing membership and privilege grids","reason":"Dedicated native grant/revoke/default-role operations remain available. Existing-family diff dispatch is Decision9. Initial members are already a create contract and use typed account records."},
  {"concept":"Protected password reveal and recovery controls","reason":"The production backend reserves encrypted expiring results before DCL and supports authenticated protected_password_result actions recover (plan_id) and reveal (reference_id, confirmed). Ordinary receipts expose references only. Shared reveal/recovery controls remain unsurfaced under Decision16; no raw key export is introduced."},
  {"concept":"Registration-dependent authentication runtimes","reason":"The audited Community source has core registration hooks but no production plugin implementing AUTH_FLAG_REQUIRES_REGISTRATION. Closed WebAuthn/Enterprise runtime integration is post beta. Native available external/socket factor lifecycle remains in beta; it is not emulated."},
  {"concept":"Membership and privilege diffs","reason":"Dedicated native grant/revoke/default-role operations remain separate. Family-editor grid dispatch remains Decision9."},
  {"concept":"Family privilege diff dispatch","reason":"Typed dedicated grant/revoke operations are declared in operations.json. Applying a family-editor cross-operation privilege diff still needs Decision9."},
  {"concept":"Account attribute state and removal","reason":"2026-11-05: ATTRIBUTE merges into the existing attributes, and MySQL removes a key only when it is sent as JSON null, which the key-value control cannot send. The attributes field is therefore an input to merge, not the account's current attributes: it does not pre-fill on reopen and offers no removal. The comment, stored as the comment attribute, does pre-fill and edit."}
 ],
